{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1785148916, "env": {"SHELL": "/usr/bin/zsh", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.02385, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J"]
[0.026193, "o", "\u001b[1;38;5;37mriverrun\u001b[0m  the anonymity layer for Solana. post-quantum.\r\n\r\n"]
[1.127263, "o", "\u001b[38;5;37m❯\u001b[0m riverrun pq\r\n"]
[1.632328, "o", "\u001b[36mriverrun: post-quantum posture\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  primitive         riverrun              curve-based tools\r\n  \u001b[2m----------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n  commitment        \u001b[1;32mBLAKE3 hash           \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31mcurve point\u001b[0m\r\n  membership proof  \u001b[1;32mRescue / FRI STARK    \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31mGroth16 / BN254\u001b[0m\r\n  trusted setup     \u001b[1;32mnone                  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31mceremony (toxic waste)\u001b[0m\r\n  under Shor        \u001b[1;32mnothing to break      \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31mkeys recovered\u001b[0m\r\n  under Grover      \u001b[1;32mhalved, absorbed      \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31mn/a\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;33mMosca's inequality:\u001b[0m  X + Y > Z  =>  you have already lost\r\n    X = years your secret must stay secret\r\n    Y = years to migrate to quantum-safe crypto  (~2)\r\n    Z = years until a quantum computer breaks today's curves  (~10)\r\n\r\n  On a \u001b[1;33mpermanent ledger\u001b[0m, X is effectively infinite: the chain is copied\r\n  forever, so any curve-based scheme fails the inequality.\r\n\r\n  riverrun is hash-based: there is no curve for Shor to attack.\r\n"]
[1.632388, "o", "  verdict: \u001b[1;32mPOST-QUANTUM\u001b[0m  what you hide today stays hidden after quantum.\r\n"]
[1.632916, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.639242, "o", "\u001b[38;5;37m❯\u001b[0m riverrun floor 30\r\n"]
[4.145782, "o", "\u001b[36mriverrun: the self-fill floor\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  Advertised k is a ceiling, not a guarantee. If an adversary self-fills\r\n  `a` of the slots (a Sybil, or a whale funding many notes), the honest\r\n  set is k - a, and effective-k falls with it.\r\n\r\n  adversary owns   honest slots    effective-k\r\n  \u001b[2m--------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n               0             30   \u001b[1;32m        30.0\u001b[0m\r\n               6             24   \u001b[1;32m        24.0\u001b[0m\r\n              12             18   \u001b[1;33m        18.0\u001b[0m\r\n              18             12   \u001b[1;31m        12.0\u001b[0m\r\n              24              6   \u001b[1;31m         6.0\u001b[0m\r\n              29              1   \u001b[1;31m         1.0\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  Owning all but one leaves you \u001b[1;31malone\u001b[0m. The defense is a per-participant\r\n  deposit cap and the funding-graph ruler, not a larger headline k.\r\n"]
[4.146317, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.154093, "o", "\u001b[38;5;37m❯\u001b[0m riverrun explain effective-k"]
[6.15416, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.660916, "o", "\u001b[36mriverrun explain: effective-k\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  effective-k is your REAL anonymity, not the advertised crowd. A pool says\r\n  you are hidden among 30. But everyone's funding source is public, so an\r\n  adversary sorts the 30 by where their money came from. If your source is\r\n  yours alone, your real crowd is 1. effective-k = 2^(entropy of that\r\n  sorting): the size of the uniform crowd that would give the same doubt.\r\n"]
[6.661589, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.669766, "o", "\u001b[38;5;37m❯\u001b[0m riverrun id show <secret> dao-vote\r\n"]
[9.174359, "o", "context: \u001b[36mdao-vote\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mshape (your identity here)\u001b[0m : a2c5287ca00d02f017fce5e397cccf30a074e5493ebbed329572055b8fda8ae8\r\n  \u001b[2mfit   (your one action)   \u001b[0m : f3a300df6589046c74f370791b458d17958eefcae8b1d122c607341a5497fc63\r\n  \u001b[2mturn  (continuity tag, ZK)\u001b[0m : 6a77233805649fc67afd3bdcca982c343ee8b59928c95b96efaf3773de8e4f0b\r\n\r\nthe same secret in another context gives a different, unlinkable shape.\r\n"]
[9.174891, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.376894, "o", "\u001b[38;5;37m❯\u001b[0m riverrun id show <secret> airdrop\r\n"]
[10.881352, "o", "context: \u001b[36mairdrop\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mshape (your identity here)\u001b[0m : c3f049f8aa7ce4ed72d0baa2da0d41f819b82ee9607278b9f03e3fb8aa24be34\r\n  \u001b[2mfit   (your one action)   \u001b[0m : 0a5cf5efb1bce200c79e12f1281a622bbb1cfbba4929132142375c55859a2e2b\r\n  \u001b[2mturn  (continuity tag, ZK)\u001b[0m : 0b560032af0bb543ac14e7fbf0ef921d041aa302a6023864187ff0e827218372\r\n\r\nthe same secret in another context gives a different, unlinkable shape.\r\n"]
[10.881962, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.084027, "o", "\u001b[38;5;244m  same secret, two contexts, two identities nobody can link back to you.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[13.686633, "o", "\u001b[1;38;5;37mmeasured privacy, post-quantum, from the terminal.\u001b[0m  full paper: paper/riverrun.pdf\r\n\r\n"]
